@node LibreClaw Troubleshooting
@section Troubleshooting

@subsection ``cmacs-podomation must be started first''

Libreclaw shares cmacs's PodEngine, so podomation must already be
running.  Either:

@example
(cmacs-podomation-start)
(cmacs-libreclaw-start)
@end example

or let @code{cmacs-libreclaw-start} auto-start podomation for you.

@subsection ``libreclaw 0.18.0 does not expose a public join-room API''

@code{cmacs-libreclaw-join-room} and @code{-leave-room} are
placeholders in the initial integration.  Add rooms to
@code{auto_join} in your YAML config and call
@code{cmacs-libreclaw-reload-config}.

@subsection ``text-read-only: LibreClaw history is read-only''

You tried to edit above the @samp{* Compose} sentinel heading.
Only the region below is writable.

@subsection Room buffer doesn't get updated

Check:

@enumerate
@item
@code{(cmacs-libreclaw-running-p)} returns @code{t}
@item
@code{(cmacs-libreclaw-list-channels)} contains the expected channel
@item
@code{(cmacs-libreclaw-channel-connected-p "CHANNEL-ID")} is @code{t}
@item
Look in @samp{*Messages*} — dispatch errors log via @code{g_warning}.
@end enumerate

@subsection @code{(gi-require "Lc" "1.0")} fails

Likely causes:

@enumerate
@item
cmacs-gi isn't built — check @code{(fboundp 'gi-require)}.
@item
The typelib isn't on @env{GI_TYPELIB_PATH}.  For in-tree builds:

@example
export GI_TYPELIB_PATH=$PWD/deps/libreclaw/build/release:$GI_TYPELIB_PATH
@end example
@end enumerate

@subsection Stale @file{.elc}/@file{.eln} after editing cmacs-libreclaw.el

The #1 cause of ``my Elisp change isn't working''.  After editing:

@example
rm -f lisp/cmacs/cmacs-libreclaw.elc \
      lisp/cmacs/cmacs-libreclaw-hatch.elc
rm -f native-lisp/*/cmacs-libreclaw-*.eln
rm -f native-lisp/*/cmacs-libreclaw-hatch-*.eln
@end example

Then restart Emacs.

@subsection Duplicate-symbol link errors after updating libreclaw

Libreclaw vendors yaml-glib and podomation inside
@file{liblc-1.0.a}.  The dedup logic in @file{src/Makefile.in}
(@code{_libreclaw_strip}) strips duplicates before linking.  If a
new libreclaw release vendors additional objects, extend
@code{_dup_yaml} / @code{_dup_podomation_objs}.

Do NOT add @code{-Wl,-z,muldefs} — that leads to non-deterministic
ABI mismatches.

@subsection Crash with ``Fatal error 6: Aborted'' in @code{signal_or_quit}

Classic @code{waiting_for_input} invariant violation.  All
C→Lisp dispatches should go through
@code{cmacs_libreclaw_dispatch_expr} (which calls
@code{cmacs_dispatch_eval} internally).  If you added a signal
handler that calls @code{Feval} or @code{call3} directly, route it
through @code{cmacs_libreclaw_dispatch_expr} instead.
